&lt;p&gt;A free and open-source, lightweight, cloud-native GIS platform for visualizing, exploring, and analyzing geospatial data. It runs everywhere you do, in the web browser, on the desktop, on mobile, and inside Jupyter notebooks, all while keeping your data local and private.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GeoLibre is built with &lt;strong&gt;Tauri v2&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;React&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;TypeScript&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;MapLibre GL JS&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;DuckDB-WASM Spatial&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;deck.gl&lt;/strong&gt;. The same workspace runs as a native desktop app, a native Android app, in any modern web browser, and adapts responsively to mobile and small screens.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://web.geolibre.app/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Launch GeoLibre Web&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; — the full app in your browser, nothing to install&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://geolibre.app/downloads/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Download the desktop app&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; — Windows, macOS, and Linux installers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=org.geolibre.app&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Get it on Google Play&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; — the native Android app&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://geolibre.app/getting-started/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Get started&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; — install, run from source, and configure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://geolibre.app/features/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Features&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; — the complete feature list&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
